Organic Chemistry tenth edition by John McMurry (@chemistry-source-organic: 0, is #reference) { r_00F02946DB1C7E37631D69129A
John E. McMurry. Organic Chemistry: A Tenth Edition. OpenStax/Rice University, published 20 September 2023; English. [Authorized publisher book](https://openstax.org/books/organic-chemistry/pages/1-why-this-chapter) and [dedication and preface](https://openstax.org/books/organic-chemistry/pages/dedication-and-preface). The actual preface identifies the tenth edition and intended two-semester introductory organic course. Current 2026 page-footer dates do not replace the publication date.

For common structural formation, read the representation/bonding preparation in chapters 1–2 as needed, then chapters 3–5 progressively with conceptual and paper-based problems. The selected passages used here are [3.2 constitutional structures and small alkane counts](https://openstax.org/books/organic-chemistry/pages/3-2-alkanes-and-alkane-isomers), [3.6 conformations](https://openstax.org/books/organic-chemistry/pages/3-6-conformations-of-ethane), [3.7 larger-alkane conformations](https://openstax.org/books/organic-chemistry/pages/3-7-conformations-of-other-alkanes), [5.1 tetrahedral enantiomers](https://openstax.org/books/organic-chemistry/pages/5-1-enantiomers-and-the-tetrahedral-carbon), [5.2 chirality](https://openstax.org/books/organic-chemistry/pages/5-2-the-reason-for-handedness-in-molecules-chirality), [5.3 optical-rotation definition](https://openstax.org/books/organic-chemistry/pages/5-3-optical-activity), [5.5 configuration rules](https://openstax.org/books/organic-chemistry/pages/5-5-sequence-rules-for-specifying-configuration), [5.7 meso distinction](https://openstax.org/books/organic-chemistry/pages/5-7-meso-compounds), the opening racemate account in [5.8](https://openstax.org/books/organic-chemistry/pages/5-8-racemic-mixtures-and-the-resolution-of-enantiomers), and [5.9 isomer classification](https://openstax.org/books/organic-chemistry/pages/5-9-a-review-of-isomerism). Section [12.7](https://openstax.org/books/organic-chemistry/pages/12-7-interpreting-infrared-spectra) supplies the bounded functional-group evidence comparison; its full spectroscopic preparation remains later reading.

On 1 November 2026, the actual publisher preface, author/date/licence metadata and the selected passages above were inspected. Common work reconstructs the small constitutional counts through six carbons, relates the single tetrahedral-center examples to an original exact model, and discusses the specific Example 12.4 functional-group comparison without copying its figures or downloading spectra. Full chapters, all exercises, solutions manuals and experiments were not audited or performed. The original programs do not implement general chemical structure elucidation or CIP nomenclature.

Keep scientific boundaries visible when reading introductory shorthand. A matching spectrum is evidence under method/sample conditions, not an unconditional uniqueness proof. A visible mirror plane is a sufficient symmetry test for a rigid structure, not a complete general search for chirality. The common block does not infer universal conformational populations or rates from a single potential-energy picture. The inspected 3.7 prose contains an inconsistent kcal/mol unit in its subtraction of two H–H contributions, whereas the adjacent table gives those contributions in kJ/mol; no numerical conformer-energy reproduction is claimed here. The optical lesson declares dm and g/mL explicitly rather than silently changing the coefficient's length unit. These reading cautions preserve what the common examples actually establish.

The current preface states CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, with component/photo attribution qualifications. Current page notices also describe additional AI-use and commercial-printing restrictions and exclude trademarks from the content licence. Identify the exact component and its notice before reuse; free access does not mean unrestricted redistribution. All textbook text, source figures, PDFs, datasets and manuals remain external. The repository provides references and original explanations/programs, with bounded attributed factual comparisons. Attempts to inspect current IUPAC Gold Book chirality/configuration entry bodies returned HTTP 403; no fresh inspection of those entries is claimed or substituted for the passages above.

The full organic-chemistry specialization remains a separate planned scope. This source's wider mechanisms, synthesis and advanced applications are not selected wholesale into the common route; later work must inspect the actual relevant material and its prerequisites.

